            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.41,
            0.887,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "The sequence of heights forms a GP with a = 18 and $r = 0.75$ (or $\\frac { 3 } { 4 } )$ , that is, 18, 13.5, 10.125, 7.594, 5.695, 4.27125, 3.2034375, … . We see that after the seventh bounce the ball remains below $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the height at which it started."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.371,
            0.539,
            0.624,
            0.569
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Exercise Set 8.3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.591,
            0.886,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "1. Find the $1 2 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ term of a GP with common ratio 2, whose $8 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ term is 192."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.634,
            0.722,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": "2. Find the $1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ and $n ^ { t h }$ terms of the GP: 5, 25, 125, … ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.658,
            0.885,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": "\\*3. A sequence is given by the recursive rule $t_{1} = 2, t_{n + 1} = 3t_{n} - 2$ for $n \\geq 1$ . Which term of the sequence is 730?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.701,
            0.886,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "4. Which term of the GP: 2, 6, 18, … is 4374? Write the explicit formula as well as the recursive formula for the $n ^ { t h }$ term."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.743,
            0.887,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "5. A ball is dropped from a height of 80 metres. After hitting the ground, it bounces back to 60% of the height from which it fell. It continues bouncing in this way — each time rising to 60% of the previous height."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.826,
            0.804,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "(i) What height does the ball reach after the $5 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ bounce?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.852,
            0.886,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": "(ii) What is the total vertical distance the ball has travelled by the time it hits the ground for the $6 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ time?"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
